# The ~50 topic-video .mp4 files at the repo root are served to portal.html
# straight from raw.githubusercontent.com (GITHUB_RAW_BASE) — nothing on the
# Vercel deployment itself ever reads them from its own domain. Every commit
# to this repo (many per day — this repo also carries admin.html/Control
# Centre) was still re-uploading all ~450MB of them into a brand new
# deployment each time, and Vercel's Hobby-plan storage quota counts every
# retained deployment's output, not just the live one — that's what pushed
# the team over its 10GB storage limit. Excluding them here doesn't touch
# git (they stay tracked, GitHub raw keeps serving them), it just stops
# Vercel from carrying dead weight it was never using.
*.mp4
# ...except the Control Centre's How-To Videos (Dale, 16 Sep 2026), which admin.html plays from this site's own
# domain (/how-to/videos). 11 short clips, about 20MB in all.
!how-to/videos/*.mp4

# DMW's own school website. GitHub Pages serves it at dmwdrivingschool.co.uk and needs it in the
# repo; Vercel only serves the Control Centre and instructor websites and must never serve it. On
# Vercel the filesystem is checked BEFORE rewrites, so while this file was deployed it answered "/"
# on every instructor subdomain - a pupil on their instructor's site landed on a rival school.
# Excluded here so "/" falls through to the rewrite that serves site.html.
index.html
